---
import AppIcon from "@/components/AppIcon.astro";
import BranchTag from "@/components/BranchTag.astro";
import HeroButton from "@/components/HeroButton.astro";
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="FnPilot">
  <div class="mx-auto flex max-w-3xl flex-col items-center px-6 py-12 text-center lg:py-20">
    <AppIcon
      lightSrc="https://images-bucket.aaron212.com/portfolio/fnpilot/FnPilot-macOS-Default-1024%401x.png"
      darkSrc="https://images-bucket.aaron212.com/portfolio/fnpilot/FnPilot-macOS-Dark-1024%401x.png"
      alt="FnPilot app icon"
      class="mb-8 w-48 lg:w-56"
      sizes="(min-width: 64rem) 14rem, 12rem"
    />
    <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-2">
      <h1 class="text-5xl font-medium lg:text-6xl">FnPilot</h1>
      <BranchTag name="Beta" tone="mint" />
    </div>
    <p class="mt-5 text-xl font-light text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 lg:text-2xl">
      Change fn key settings based on the frontmost window.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap justify-center gap-4">
      <HeroButton label="Releases" href="https://github.com/Aaron-212/FnPilot/releases/latest" variant="primary" />
      <HeroButton label="Check it on GitHub" href="https://github.com/Aaron-212/FnPilot" variant="secondary" />
    </div>
    <p class="p-4 text-slate-500">Requires macOS 26.0 or later | Universal Binary</p>
  </div>
  <div class="prose mx-auto max-w-3xl select-auto dark:prose-invert lg:prose-lg">
    <p>
      FnPilot is a macOS menu bar app for switching the keyboard function-key mode globally or per application. Keep
      media controls in most apps and use standard F1–F12 keys in terminals, editors, IDEs, or games.
    </p>
    <h2>Features</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Switch between Media and Fn modes from the menu bar.</li>
      <li>Use Media mode for brightness, volume, playback, and other media controls.</li>
      <li>Use Fn mode for standard function keys.</li>
      <li>Set per-app overrides that follow the foreground app.</li>
      <li>Choose which mode stays active after quitting FnPilot.</li>
      <li>Add rules for application bundles and standalone executable paths.</li>
      <li>Launch at login and store preferences locally.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Release downloads</h2>
    <p>
      GitHub releases contain unsigned app bundles. macOS may block the first launch or show an unidentified developer
      warning. If you trust the source, use Finder’s Open command or the privacy controls in System Settings to allow
      the app.
    </p>
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <p>
      FnPilot runs in the menu bar without opening its settings window at launch. After waking from sleep or returning
      to your user session, it reads the system keyboard mode and reapplies the foreground app’s rule or the global
      mode. It pauses rule application while asleep or while another user session is active.
    </p>
    <p>
      Changes in System Settings don’t update FnPilot’s saved preferences. They can remain active until you switch apps,
      wake your Mac, return to your user session, or edit a FnPilot rule. FnPilot then reapplies the applicable rule; it
      doesn’t continuously monitor System Settings.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
